<article class="env-proposition" id="0EI2">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0EI2">Proposition <span data-tag="0EI2">51.14.2</span>.</a> Let $A$ be a Noetherian ring which has a dualizing complex. Let $T \subset \mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(A)$ be a subset stable under specialization. Let $s \in \mathbf{Z}$. Let $K \in D_{\textit{Coh}}^+(A)$. The following are equivalent </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
$H^ i_ T(K)$ is a finite $A$-module for $i \leq s$, and 
</p>
</li><li><p>
for all $\mathfrak p \not\in T$, $\mathfrak q \in T$ with $\mathfrak p \subset \mathfrak q$ we have 
</p>
<div class="equation">
  \[  \text{depth}_{A_\mathfrak p}(K_\mathfrak p) + \dim ((A/\mathfrak p)_\mathfrak q) > s  \]
</div>
</li>
</ol></p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Formal consequence of Proposition <a href="/tag/0EHZ" data-tag="0EHZ">51.13.2</a> and Lemma <a href="/tag/0EI1" data-tag="0EI1">51.14.1</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>